// #71/#72 round, layer 2 — ADMIT half, and the ONE VARIABLE against the
// dangle twin is whether the CALLEE RETAINS its argument. Everything else is
// byte-identical: same fat `str` by-value argument, same `MethodCall` node,
// same dying `owner`, same use of the result afterwards.
//
// `my_as_str3` returns a static literal, so its summary is `result<-0` and
// `arg_retained_by_callee` answers false — no tie, admitted. That is the
// tv_build exemption stated BY CONSTRUCTION rather than by a fat-versus-plain
// guess: the two fixtures cannot be separated by the argument's TYPE (it is
// the same `str`) nor by the result's (also the same), only by what the
// callee DOES. The companion pin
// tests/logos/pass/bc_argcomp_tvbuild_byvalue_fat_admit.logos holds the same
// line for a `#[borrow_carrying]` result.
package bc_fatret_nested_call_admit;
use logos.mem.string;

pub fn my_as_str3(s: &str) -> str { return "abcde"; }

fn main() -> i32 {
    let v: str;
    {
        let owner: String = String::from("hello");
        v = my_as_str3(owner.as_str());
    }
    // The use is what asks the §B6 liveness question, and it now asserts the
    // VALUE too: `len() >= 0` was a tautology forced by #80 (a deferred-init
    // `str` assigned inside a block read a wrong length — 1 for a 5-byte
    // literal). #80 is fixed (declare_local_place), so the debt is paid and
    // the fixture pins the real answer: `my_as_str3` returns "abcde".
    let n: i64 = v.len();
    if n == 5i64 { return 0i32; }
    return 1i32;
}
